  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-wallpaper",
      "text": "[](LICENSE)\n\nA **wallpaper / background plugin** for the [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) Web UI. Add a background image to the harness window that **auto-adapts to any screen**: the image is scaled with CSS `cover`, so it looks right on 1080p, 2K, 4K, or any display scaling, and the translucent surface colors follow light/dark theme automatically."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-wallpaper",
      "text": "Built-in preset enabled by default, custom image URL support, and an opacity slider — all from the **Settings → General → Wallpaper** row, with no Host restart and no plugin configuration."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- 🌄 **Built-in preset on by default** — the bundled \"Origami\" wallpaper (2560×1440) is applied immediately on a fresh profile\n- 🖼️ **Custom image URLs** — paste any same-origin path (`/wallpapers/xxx.jpg`) or full `https://…` URL and hit Apply\n- 🔄 **On/off switch** — one click to toggle the background\n- 🎚️ **Opacity slider** — 30%–100% surface translucency, with separate values for light and dark themes\n- 📐 **Any screen** — CSS `cover` scales and centers the image regardless of resolution, window size, or display scaling\n- ⚡ **Pure client-side** — persists via `localStorage`, no Host schema registration, no `dsh web` restart, HMR-friendly"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "From this repository:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin add https://github.com/fubao885522/dsh-wallpaper\n```\n\nFrom this checkout (development):\n\n```sh\npnpm install\npnpm build\ncd ..\ndsh plugin add ./dsh-wallpaper\n\nRemove:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin remove dsh-wallpaper\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "1. Open **Settings → General**.\n2. Find the **Wallpaper** row (below Appearance).\n3. Click **Origami** to apply the built-in preset, or paste an image URL and click **Apply**.\n4. Use the toggle to turn the background on/off and the slider to adjust translucency.\n\nThe setting is stored per browser (`localStorage`), so it survives page reloads and HMR reloads."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it adapts to any machine",
      "text": "- The image is rendered with `background-size: cover; background-position: center`, so any resolution, aspect ratio, or DPI scaling is handled automatically.\n- Surface colors are written as the same `--dsw-alias-*` tokens the harness frame uses, made translucent; `body[data-ds-dark-theme]` selects the dark palette values, so readability holds in both themes.\n- Opacity is clamped to a readable range (0.3–1.0) and stored as a plain number."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "| Plugin | DeepSeek Harness |\n|---|---|\n| `0.1.x` | `0.1.0-rc.5` / `0.1.0-rc.6` (Web GUI) |"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
